## IMPORTANT Session Start Protocol

### Unconditional (run on EVERY session, regardless of what user says)

1. MUST Read `.claude/lessons.md` — behavioral corrections from past sessions
2. MUST Run `mcp__nexus__session_briefing()` — graph stats, stale docs, coverage gaps, recent changes
3. MUST read and follow the development guide at docs/development.rst
4. MUST load vv-principles skill — provides the V&V framework (hierarchy, failure modes,
   anti-patterns, three pillars, bug-logging directive) that all sub-agents preload via their
   AGENT.md skills: list. Loading puts you at parity with the agents you'll dispatch.
5. MUST load subagent-handoff-protocol skill — provides the agent table (who does what +
   preloaded skills) AND the DISPATCH_REQUEST / DISPATCH_RESULT protocol that lets sub-agents
   coordinate via you as the bridge (sub-agents cannot dispatch other sub-agents per Anthropic
   constraint). You orchestrate; sub-agents have depth, you have breadth. Optional augmentation
   block lets you append additional context-aware questions to a brief before dispatch without
   modifying the requesting sub-agent's original brief.

### On task identification (as soon as the user states what ORPHEUS module to work on)

6. MUST check GitHub Issues: `gh issue list -l module:<name>`
7. Dispatch the **explorer** agent on that module for a detailed picture



