## SESSION START PROTOCOL — execute as your FIRST tool-call batch

> Run these in parallel as the first response of any new session,
> BEFORE addressing the user's first message. They are pre-load
> equivalents — main-agent counterpart of sub-agent skill preloads.

In a single message, dispatch these tool calls in parallel:

1. `Skill: vv-principles`
2. `Skill: subagent-handoff-protocol`
3. `Read .claude/lessons.md`
4. `mcp__nexus__session_briefing()`
5. `Read docs/development.rst`

Then respond to the user's first message. If their first message
is trivially short (a greeting, a clarifying question), still
execute the batch — its cost is < 5 seconds and it grounds
EVERY subsequent action.
